    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22593" root="شغو and شغى" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْغَى</span></b> ; fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَغْوَآءُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَغْيَآءُ</span>; and pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُغْوٌ</span>: see
1, last sentence. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَغْوَآءُ</span> also signifies <i>An eagle;</i>
(S, Msb, K;) because its upper mandible exceeds
the lower: (S, Msb:) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُّ شَغْوَة</span></b> . (T in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ام</span>.)

